"""Silverpine North: story speeches, and places named where the old accept line used to carry them."""

STORY = {
    'spn_worg_cull': ("Now you've walked it, you'll have seen the verge.\n\nThe worgs have moved onto it. They aren't in the road. They're on the verge, the strip of scrub either side, where a thing can pace a cart for half a mile without ever being in the open. That's hunting behaviour, it's new this season, and I've lost two carts to it this month.\n\nAnd the ghouls have come in behind them, because a worg pack leaves a great deal behind and a ghoul isn't proud. So now there are two problems on that strip, and the second exists entirely because of the first.\n\nPush them both back off the verges of the Trunk Road. Start with the worgs. Take their leavings away, and the ghouls will follow the food elsewhere.", "Leave their dens alone if you find them. It's the verge I need, not the whole wood."),
    'spn_pell_glands': ("You'll be the one Vesk keeps sending into the woods. I'm Apothecary Pell, and I've got a requisition and no one to requisition.\n\nI want Silverpine spider venom. Properly cut and properly reduced, I believe it can be made to slow the Plague rather than feed it, which isn't a thing anyone in the Undercity wants to hear me say out loud.\n\nI've got a great many theories, and most of them have been wrong. This one can be tested with things that can be killed and weighed, rather than argued about in a chamber by people who've never cut anything.\n\nThe Skittering Dark, far south-east of this gate, is nothing but spiders, so get me the glands there. Bring them intact, if you can manage it, because a burst one is worth nothing but mess.", "Cut them out with the sac still closed. One drop of that on your skin and you'll know why."),
}

# places named where the old accept line used to carry them
STORY['spn_trunk_walk'] = ("I'm Captain Vesk, of the Forsaken Rear Guard. This gate is the border, and that road is the only reason the gate matters.\n\nThe Trunk Road runs from here to the Crossroads and on to the Sepulcher. Everything we have in Silverpine comes up it: orders, relief, the carts, the occasional person who actually knows something. Cut the road, and this garrison stops being a border post and becomes a building full of men in a wood.\n\nNobody has walked the whole length of it since the first frost. We patrol the first mile and the Sepulcher patrols their end, and in between there's a stretch that exists on my map and nowhere else.\n\nWalk all of it, south to the crossroads in the middle of the forest. Then come back and tell me what my map is wrong about.", None)
STORY['spn_muckmaw'] = ("It's in the Shadowspring Pools, east of here, in the deep pool at the back that doesn't reflect anything.\n\nThere's something in it. It's old, older than the springs turning, I think, and that isn't a thing I say lightly. It took Hest in the spring and it took Dorn in the autumn, and both times there was no struggle at all. They were at the bank, and then they weren't.\n\nThe locals call it Muckmaw, which makes it sound like a story for children. I've let them keep calling it that, because the alternative is explaining to a patrol that there's something in my pools that eats a Forsaken without waking the water.\n\nKill it for me. I've run out of scouts and patience, in roughly that order.", None)
STORY['spn_sd_longleg'] = ("Longleg is the one that takes a hunter a week.\n\nIt's the size of a cart. I want you to hold that in your head rather than nodding past it, because everyone nods past it, and then they see it and stop thinking clearly at exactly the wrong moment.\n\nIt doesn't web. It stalks, properly stalks. It matches your pace, stays off the path, and comes when you've stopped moving and started looking at something else. I've got three apprentices' worth of experience in that sentence, and I'd rather not get a fourth.\n\nIt'll be in the Skittering Dark, east of here, on the high ground off the Skittering road. Go slowly, don't stop in the open, and don't look at anything for long.", None)
